  "scope": "Final-step damage aggregation has a conservative eligibility guard. It requires a clean move boundary, one remaining Pokemon per side, no weather, no HP-damaging status, no unapproved volatile/side/field effect, and whitelisted moves and item callbacks. Sleep Talk requires all potential called moves to be approved. Approved attacks hit once, have HP-independent power, and cannot cause recoil, drain, confusion or residual damage. Within a damage bucket, subsequent predicates are KO, Focus Band, or healing thresholds already retained by ThresholdLean; the representative is consumed at the horizon and is never used for future strategic decisions. Rejected cells use the previous exact streaming/eager path. All executed cells are audited against the native kernel, comparing four outcome categories only for projected final-step cells. All ledgers and controller decisions are independently verified. Two runs per backend and zero/500ms controls are included. A 720-case HP/item/move grid checks eligible projections; unsafe move/status controls are rejected, and the sandstorm counterexample uses the exact fallback. This is a source-reviewed eligibility argument and finite testing, not a machine-checked proof for every engine state. Runtime excludes audits, loading and model replay. Production integration and deployed-bot superiority are not established."
